-- A regression guard (checker-v2.md §9.5):
-- `x == [ x ]` makes `x`'s type contain itself. The resolver walk that
-- meets the cycle reports it ONCE, at the `==`, and poisons the cycle's root,
-- so the `<` on the same receiver adds nothing. The cycle is written as its
-- structure, `a = List a`, never as `a  =  … a …`.
f x =
    x == [ x ] && x < [ x ]
